     "On Friday, July 19, 2013 11:15:32 PM UTC-4, Carlos wrote:<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">But in your case, A is diagonal so the log determinant is just sum(log(A1)) which is much faster than doing anything on an arbitrary positive definite matrix.</blockquote><div><br></div></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>Mmmmm nope, A is not diagonal. I create first an identity matrix, but then I assign also some values in the off-diagonal cells. The idea is that A in general is not diagonal. The off-diagonal values represent the restrictions on the contemporaneous relationships among the variables in y.</div></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote><div><br><div><div><div><div>I said the wrong thing. In your example,<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><pre><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// Build matrix A</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    A           </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> diag_matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rep_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span></pre></div></code></div><br>A is lower-triangular, in which case its log determinant is still 2 * sum(log(A1)). So, I was wrong to say that it was diagonal but the expression for its log determinant is the same as if it were diagonal. But if in your real problem, A is not triangular, then go ahead and use Marcus&#39; log_determinant() function.<br><br>Ben<br> <br></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Djx6LlPWI7AJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2013-07-20T04:06:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: Changes in lp__ for a structural VAR model",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Friday, July 19, 2013 10:32:01 PM UTC-4, Ben Goodrich wrote:"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Second, if H is diagonal, then you don&#39;t want to call any variant of multi_normal(). Instead subtract<br><div><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">(A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">) -</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> (C </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))) ./ H1 )</span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></code></div></div></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><br>That should have said<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dot_self</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">A</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">./</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> H1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></span></code></div></code></div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>Then,\r\n you have to account for the log determinant of H * H&#39; , which is just 2\r\n * sum(log(H1)) but is multiplied by -1/2 in the multinormal \r\nlog-likelihood.<br><br>So, I think it should be<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">lp__ &lt;- lp__ + sum(log(A1)) - </span><code><span style=\"color:#000\">dot_self</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><code><span style=\"color:#000\">(A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">) -</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> (C </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))) ./ H1 ) - </span></code></code>sum(log(H1));</div></code></div></div></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div> <br>and thus the last line should be <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\"><span style=\"color:#000\">lp__ </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp__ </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">A1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dot_self</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">A</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C </span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">col</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">./</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> H1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span></code></code><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">H1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span></div></code></div></div></code></div><br>Ben<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
